cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Receipts or its study of 181 real changes, please cite it as below."
title: "Receipts: checks that a change's tests would have caught the bug it fixes"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: syntaxixr
    website: "https://github.com/syntaxixr"
repository-code: "https://github.com/syntaxixr/receipts"
url: "https://github.com/syntaxixr/receipts/blob/main/docs/study.md"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-26"
keywords:
  - testing
  - regression tests
  - coding agents
  - claude code
  - pytest
  - vitest
  - jest
abstract: >-
  Receipts runs every test a change adds or edits twice: with the change, and
  with the changed source files reverted to the base branch. A test for a fix
  must fail without it. A study over 81 maintainer fix commits and 100 pull
  requests with coding-agent fingerprints found 90% and 82% proven; in 10% of
  agent pull requests every test failed on the old code only because it
  imported a name the change added.
